THOUGHT: Other code paths call root.getMethodUtils() and use it directly, suggesting it’s intended to be non-null. Here, only this visitor stores it in a nullable field and dereferences it, triggering NullAway. The safest minimal fix is to guard the dereference with a null check and simply skip attaching details if methodUtils is unavailable. I’ll update AttachMethodDetails.attachMethodDetails to return early when methodUtils is null, then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '44,48c\	private void attachMethodDetails(BaseInvokeNode insn) {
		MethodUtils mu = this.methodUtils;
		if (mu == null) {
			return;
		}
		IMethodDetails methodDetails = mu.getMethodDetails(insn.getCallMth());
		if (methodDetails != null) {
			insn.addAttr(methodDetails);
		}
	}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/AttachMethodDetails.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

